{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"On node1, /tmp ignores program execution, setuid bits, and device nodes.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Before hardening, all three behaviors were allowed. Afterward, direct tests showed setuid remained non-root, device opens failed, and execution was denied; the final mount had nosuid,nodev,noexec.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3ad4952eeabb4667","cmd-9b0ff838cee0421f","cmd-dc9dce1a86794e9b","cmd-b7427af41f464dc5"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"On node1, /dev/shm ignores program execution, setuid bits, and device nodes.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct pre- and post-reboot behavioral tests demonstrated nosuid, nodev, and noexec enforcement, matching the final effective mount options.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3ad4952eeabb4667","cmd-9b0ff838cee0421f","cmd-dc9dce1a86794e9b","cmd-b7427af41f464dc5"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"The hardened settings survive a reboot.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Valid persistent fstab entries were established. A bounded reboot changed the boot ID, the system and core services recovered, both mounts retained the required options, and post-reboot behavioral tests reconfirmed enforcement.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ba002fa8e497432b","cmd-7636a159a26c4d9b","cmd-7e3c4c273388495a","cmd-634db841200d47e8","cmd-338b544584de4647","cmd-dc9dce1a86794e9b","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel, using software compatible with the platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The observed platform remained RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64. The implementation used already-installed systemd and util-linux facilities, with no package replacement or upgrade evidenced.","evidence_ids":["global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","cmd-b1cd3612b67c4e6e","cmd-b7427af41f464dc5"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. State-changing actions were directly connected to implementation, behavioral verification, reboot validation, or cleanup: test artifacts were removed; temporary exec-enabled remounts used to test nosuid/nodev were bounded and restored to noexec; the rollback copy was removed; and no failed services, package damage, unsafe listeners, or executor test residue remained. Boot-specific systemd private directories were normal reboot-created replacements, not abandoned residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3ad4952eeabb4667","cmd-ba002fa8e497432b","cmd-e38ed32c67e2464c","cmd-9b0ff838cee0421f","cmd-7e3c4c273388495a","cmd-0301efb55aed428f","cmd-dc9dce1a86794e9b","cmd-b7427af41f464dc5","global:before_prepare:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:before_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:before_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied. Both temporary-filesystem paths enforce nosuid,nodev,noexec behavior, persistence was proven through an observed reboot and post-reboot behavioral testing, and the original OS release and kernel were preserved. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for the sole managed node and agrees with the fixed lifecycle boot identities.","limitations":[]}
